The probability that all four dice show the same number is calculated by considering that the first die can be any number, and each subsequent die must match the first. This gives $1 \times \frac{1}{6} \times \frac{1}{6} \times \frac{1}{6} = \frac{1}{216}$. Subtracting this from 1 gives the probability that they are not all the same:

$$
1 - \frac{1}{216} = \frac{215}{216}
$$

**Answer:** \boxed{\dfrac{215}{216}}

